 "workflowNote": "Small text and data edits go to cheap OpenRouter models: gpt-4.1 writes whole files and has passed every task given so far; a smaller model handles one-file edits well but sometimes replies in chat instead of editing, so its failures move to gpt-4.1. Codex builds pass their gates more often at higher effort, and runs stopped by the weekly quota are no longer counted against it. Claude keeps design, review and judgment work; Sonnet fix tasks on shared lesson code failed most often, so those now go to a designer first. Most Claude rows before 22 October did not record the model, so their pass rates are estimates."
